# CAN Frame Contracts

## Reconcile across every device, every time

**Read `docs/RECONCILIATION-RULES.md` Rule 2 before finalizing any CAN change.** A CAN change
on any one device is not done until it has been reconciled against **all** the others:

| Device | Config lives in |
|---|---|
| Link G4X XtremeX ECU | `link_g4x_can_setup.json`, `.lcs`, `CANBUS-LINK-G4X-CONFIG.md` |
| Center cluster ESP32-P4 | `center-cluster-esp32-p4` repo — `main/canbus.c`, `main/protocols/link_g4x.json` |
| RealDash | `link_g4x_realdash.xml`, `st185_dash.rd`, `REALDASH-LAYOUT.md`, `rd-build/` |
| ECUMaster CSB3 switchboard | `ECUMASTER_SWITCHBOARD_SETUP.md` |
| Link CAN-Lambda | On the same bus — see below |

This crosses repository boundaries. A change here that affects the cluster is not complete
until the cluster side is checked, even though it lives in another repo.

For every frame touched, confirm across all participants: frame ID, byte offsets, field
widths, endianness, scaling, offset, units, and which device transmits vs receives.

## Bus facts

- **Link CAN-Lambda is on CAN bus 1**, with everything else. Not a separate bus.
- **CAN bus 2 is unused.** Its ECU pins are free for any purpose — do not reserve them.
- Single bus, 1 Mbit/s.

## Authority order

1. **Center cluster firmware as flashed** — highest, and it is **frozen**.
2. PCLink CAN configuration on the ECU.
3. Everything else.

Frozen means the *other* device changes when there is a conflict. Reflashing the cluster is a
last resort and requires explicit approval from Daniel — never do it just to clear a mismatch.

## Contract details

- Keep frame IDs `0x3E8`-`0x3F1` and `0x640`-`0x643` consistent with `link_g4x_can_setup.json`.
- Keep CAN ID usage and field sizing consistent between `bench/frames.py` and
  `link_g4x_can_setup.json`.
- Preserve BigEndian for multibyte fields unless a canonical doc changes it.
- Keep warning-bit definitions in sync with the `WARN_*` constants in `bench/frames.py`.
- RealDash receives the ECU-owned `0x3EF`-`0x3F1` frames and does **not** read the switchboard
  `0x640`-`0x642` directly.
- Validate with targeted `bench/can_bench.py` command paths before finalizing.

If a mismatch is found and not fixed in the same pass, write it down as an open item. Never
leave it silent.
